%% Filter decision — Eventing Deep-Dive & Serverless Workflows.
%% What a Trigger filter actually decides, drawn from the Demo page's filtering step: that step sends
%% a com.parasol.claim.rejected event, the catch-all Trigger claims-events has no filter and delivers
%% it, and claims-fraud-review filters on type=com.parasol.claim.submitted, does not match, and drops
%% it. The consumer logs ONE delivery for that event rather than two, and the count is the filter at
%% work. Deliberately ONE event, not both the step sends: a second event doubles every rank and the
%% picture stops answering "what does this filter decide".
%% ---
%% Authored 2026-09-12 for that step, which until now borrowed 03-what-you-built (the end-state
%% recap). Colors carry the same meaning as 01-eventing-model.mmd — amber producer, blue broker,
%% green triggers, light-blue sink — plus the red class from 02-retries-dlq.mmd on the branch where
%% nothing is delivered.
%% ---
%% NEVER put an angle-bracket placeholder in a .mmd file. Antora emits mermaid source into the page
%% UNESCAPED, so a word wrapped in angle brackets becomes a REAL DOM element that swallows the rest
%% of the graph, and mermaid then renders "Syntax error in text" while the Antora build still exits 0.
%% The line-break tag is the only markup safe inside a label, at most two per label. Second trap, same
%% symptom: a BARE "%%" line with no text after it defeats mermaid's comment stripper and the leftover
%% marker merges into the next line — every comment line here ends in text, separators are "%% ---".
%% ---
%% No subgraphs on purpose: this is four ranks and two outcomes, and a subgraph whose `direction` is
%% silently discarded by an edge crossing its boundary is how these diagrams become tall columns.
flowchart LR
  E(["one event: claim.rejected<br/>POSTed to the broker"])
  B[("Broker: default<br/>accepts it — HTTP 202")]
  T1{"claims-events<br/>no filter — matches everything"}
  T2{"claims-fraud-review<br/>filter: type=claim.submitted"}
  C["claims-consumer<br/>displays it — one delivery"]
  X["no match: this trigger drops it<br/>nothing delivered, and no error"]
  E --> B
  B --> T1
  B --> T2
  T1 ==>|"delivers"| C
  T2 -.->|"filtered out"| X
  classDef src fill:#fef7e0,stroke:#b06000,color:#7a4100;
  classDef hub fill:#e8eaf6,stroke:#3949ab,color:#1a237e;
  classDef trig fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  classDef sink fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0,color:#0d47a1;
  classDef bad fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#a50e0e;
  class E src; class B hub; class T1,T2 trig; class C sink; class X bad;
